Description: Browse push: shows a hidden library, held opens the search, no load
 [Library],GoToItem (the browse encoder push of many controller mappings):
 - while the skin hides the library ([Skin],show_maximized_library 0 and the
   library widget not visible) a push sets show_maximized_library to 1, so
   the library page appears at the list shown last; it acts on nothing
   nobody can see;
 - a push held for one second opens the search: the library is shown, the
   search box gets the focus and [Library],search_request (new, read only)
   counts up, so a skin can switch to the list it searches. This needs the
   release (GoToItem 0): the push then acts on release. Until a mapping has
   sent a release, every push acts at once, as before;
 - in the track table a push loads nothing (Mixxx: the double-click action,
   e.g. into the first stopped deck); each deck has its own LOAD.
 Numark Mixtrack Pro 3: the browse push sends GoToItem's release too.
 Skins that always show the library are unchanged apart from the hold and
 the track table.
Author: DecksmithOS
Forwarded: no
Last-Update: 2026-11-24
---
